::: {.cell}

Hodgkin lymphoma is characterized by the diagnostic **Reed-Sternberg cell** -- a large binucleated or multilobated cell with prominent inclusion-like nucleoli, set within a reactive background of T cells, eosinophils, plasma cells, and macrophages. Subtypes include: Nodular Sclerosis (collagen bands, lacunar cells), Mixed Cellularity (abundant RS cells), Lymphocyte-Rich, Lymphocyte-Depleted, and Nodular Lymphocyte Predominant (popcorn/L&H cells without classic RS cells).
